nodes.body:
@jeejeelee I reworked this based on your review. restored the default `split_k` selection and tuned-config behavior.

While validating the opt-in path, found and fixed a separate FP8 gap: block-wise FP8 shrink changed `BLOCK_K` at 128 tokens, which changed the same row's output. The direct reproducer is now bit-exact across 31–129 tokens.

Could you take another look when you have time? Thanks!

